This distribution uses third-party software. The project license does not
replace the licenses of these components. Their copyright/license/notice
texts accompany this distribution in docs/third-party-licenses/.

docs/third-party-windows.json lists the active Windows Cargo target graph,
including build dependencies. It is broader than the code linked into either
individual executable; it excludes inactive optional Cargo dependencies.
The native Skia PDF/codecs/text library has additional pinned notices listed
in docs/skia-native-notices.json and docs/third-party-licenses/skia-native/.
The conservative native notice collection includes optional codec modules;
it does not assert that every listed module is linked.

Principal components include kurbo, linesweeper, resvg/usvg/harfrust,
eframe/egui/winit, image/zune-jpeg, serde, sha2, unicode-segmentation and
rust-skia/Skia. Refer to the versioned inventories for all resolved packages.

The egui default UI fonts include OFL-1.1 and Ubuntu-font-1.0 licensed fonts.
Their notices are included with epaint_default_fonts. Document fonts are read
from the user's operating system; no Microsoft or Apple system font files
are included. Synthetic example PNG/JPEG fixtures are project-generated.

No Graphite or Inkscape executable/source is included in this distribution.
No LLM, account, cloud service, toolchain, SDK or Python runtime is bundled.
